@page "/docs/direction"
@using Blaizio.Docs.Examples.Direction
<PageTitle>Direction (RTL) - Blaizio</PageTitle>

<div class="typeset typeset-docs space-y-10">
    <header class="docs-page-header space-y-2.5">
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
            <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">Direction (RTL)</h1>
            <BzBadge Variant="BadgeVariant.Secondary">logical CSS</BzBadge>
            <BzBadge Variant="BadgeVariant.Outline">keyboard mirroring</BzBadge>
        </div>
        <p>Every Blaizio component follows the reading direction. Set it for the whole app with <code>dir</code> on <code>&lt;html&gt;</code>, or for one region with <code>DirectionProvider</code>. The styling mirrors through logical CSS properties, and the left and right arrow keys swap along with it. To see it on this whole site, use the LTR/RTL switch in the top bar.</p>
    </header>

    <UsageBlock Example="typeof(DirectionUsageExample)"
                Description="Wrap any part of the tree in a `DirectionProvider` and everything inside follows its direction. Spacing, alignment and arrow-key navigation all mirror." />

    <ExamplesHeading />

    <Demo Title="Scoped to a subtree" Description="A `DirectionProvider` flips only its own children. The icon side, text alignment, tab order and arrow keys mirror inside it, while the rest of the page is unchanged."
          Example="typeof(DirectionScopedExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Per-component override" Description="Put a `dir` attribute on a single component to override the surrounding direction for that component alone."
          Example="typeof(DirectionPerComponentExample)" />

    <section>
        <h2 data-toc class="scroll-mt-20">How it works</h2>
        <p>Direction is expressed as the standard <code>dir</code> attribute in the DOM. <code>DirectionProvider</code> sets it on a wrapper that does not affect layout, and two things follow from that one attribute:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>CSS logical properties such as padding, borders and alignment mirror.</li>
            <li>The script that handles arrow-key focus movement reads the current direction and swaps Left and Right.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>You can get the same result with a raw <code>dir="rtl"</code> on any component, or, on a headless primitive, by passing <code>Dir="Direction.Rtl"</code>.</p>
    </section>
</div>

